  ],
  "difficulty": 4,
  "marks": 1,
  "estimatedSeconds": 90,
  "stem": "The line $y = 2x + 1$ meets the curve $y = x^{2} - 2$ at the points $A$ and $B$. Find the length of $AB$, correct to 3 significant figures.",
  "answerSpec": {
   "value": 8.94427190999916,
   "tolerance": {
    "kind": "absolute",
    "amount": 0.005
   }
  },
  "explanation": "$x^{2} - 2 = 2x + 1$ gives $x^{2} - 2x - 3 = 0$, so $x = -1$ or $3$: $A(-1, -1)$, $B(3, 7)$. $AB = \\sqrt{4^{2} + 8^{2}} = \\sqrt{80} = 4\\sqrt{5} = 8.94$.",
  "workedSolution": "1. Equate: $x^{2} - 2 = 2x + 1$, so $x^{2} - 2x - 3 = 0$.\n2. $(x - 3)(x + 1) = 0$: $x = 3$ or $x = -1$.\n3. From the line: $A(-1, -1)$ and $B(3, 7)$.\n4. $AB = \\sqrt{(3 - (-1))^{2} + (7 - (-1))^{2}} = \\sqrt{16 + 64} = \\sqrt{80}$.\n5. $AB = 4\\sqrt{5} = 8.94$ (3 s.f.).",
  "hints": [
   "Find both intersection points first.",
   "Distance = √[(x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²]."
  ],
  "modelResponse": {
   "type": "CALCULATION",
   "value": "8.94"
  },
